<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vaduz Castle</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vaduz Castle stands on a terrace above Vaduz, the capital of Liechtenstein. Built in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and enlarged by the counts of Werdenberg-Sargans and their successors, it was burnt by Swiss troops in 1499 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-war">Swabian War</a>. Restored in the early 20th century, it has been the residence of the princes of Liechtenstein since 1938.</p></div>
